To fix this vulnerability, you can modify the path_f function to check if the path contains any.. (dot dot) characters and reject it if it does. Here is an example of how you can do this:

function path_f ($path)
{
    global $home_dir;
    $abs_dir = $home_dir;
    switch ($path)
    {
        case ".":
        case "": return realpath($abs_dir);

        default:
